.oh-my-zsh/

# Machine-specific kanshi profiles — monitor make/model/serial must not land in this
# public repo. Stowed alongside the tracked skeleton, which `include`s them.
# The directory stays tracked via 00-placeholder.conf, which must be a REAL .conf and not a
# .gitkeep: kanshi hard-errors when the include glob matches nothing, and `*` does not match a
# dot-prefixed name — so a .gitkeep left kanshi refusing to start at all. See that file.
config-stow/kanshi/kanshi/config.d/*
!config-stow/kanshi/kanshi/config.d/00-placeholder.conf

# Machine-/device-specific niri overrides — real output blocks, custom xkb keymap path,
# Bluetooth device MAC binds. Optionally `include`d by the tracked config.kdl skeleton;
# supplied per-machine (or by the private machine-config repo). Same reasoning as kanshi.
config-stow/niri/.config/niri/local.kdl

# DMS matugen output. `matugenTemplateKitty: true` in the shared DMS baseline regenerates
# these from the current theme, and ~/.config/kitty is a SYMLINK to this directory — so DMS
# writes them straight into the working tree, on every machine, every time the theme changes.
# Generated machine-local state, not configuration: ignored rather than tracked.
#
# NOTHING READS THEM TODAY: kitty.conf has no `include` line at all, so these are generated
# and then dropped on the floor. Either add `include dank-theme.conf` / `include dank-tabs.conf`
# to the tracked kitty.conf (the palette follows DMS, and these stay ignored), or set
# matugenTemplateKitty to false and stop generating them. Leaving it as-is is the one option
# that keeps producing untracked noise for no benefit.
config-stow/terminals/.config/kitty/dank-theme.conf
config-stow/terminals/.config/kitty/dank-tabs.conf
